# Line endings are load-bearing in this project, not cosmetic.
#
# `runtime/policy_development.validate_policy_source` rejects a policy whose
# entry file does not use LF, and the Pi adapter speaks strict LF-delimited
# JSONL. On Windows, git's default `core.autocrlf` would rewrite these files to
# CRLF on checkout and silently break both. Pin LF for everything, so the
# working tree, the index and any future clone all agree with what is on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets that must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.sqlite3 binary
